#: healthcheck_system/mmc_life.py:120
msgid ""
"MMC storage has limited amount of writes and because of that it has "
"limited lifespan. This means that this is normal and expected if your "
"device is cheap or years old. In case of new device it can be either "
"faulty from factory or more likely it was used very heavily in the past. "
"Note that most of the manufacturers do not provide warranty if MMC was "
"used heavily.\n"
msgstr ""

#: healthcheck_system/mmc_life.py:126
msgid ""
"To prolong device lifespan you should minimize amount of writes "
"(preferably to only system updates). This means moving any write heavy "
"tasks such as file sharing, databases, containers, logs and others to "
"some other storage storage device."
msgstr ""

